 orders exactly the forecast. Average demand is about 4.6% higher than the forecast, so there are some lost sales. A small stock buffer still builds up from day-to-day variation.\n- Candidate 4 orders about 12–15% above the forecast, roughly 185 extra units costing about 1,800. Those units recover about 2,000 in sales and penalties. However, the surplus keeps piling up, which adds holding cost and leftover stock at the end. On balance candidate 3 comes out slightly ahead, but it is close.\n\n**Every-other-day plans.**\n- Candidate 5 (about 1.05× forecast) matches average demand, so it is the strongest of this group.\n- Candidate 2 orders exactly the forecast, so it runs slightly short.\n- Candidates 1, 6 and 7 order 1.1–1.3× the forecast and end up overstocked.\n\n**Robustness.** When actual demand moves away from the forecast, plans ordering about the average amount (3, 5, 2) hold up best. The plans that over-order lose more to holding and to stock left over at the end.\n\n| Candidate | Probability |\n|---|---|\n| 0 | 0.04 |\n| 1 | 0.10 |\n| 2 | 0.15 |\n| 3 | 0.25 |\n| 4 | 0.13 |\n| 5 | 0.22 |\n| 6 | 0.07 |\n| 7 | 0.04 |"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4384, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2305, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4384}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T21:41:01.257Z", "request_id": "req_011CgVMrdoxxGkgy5TsqsJCG"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01VdWMxib32aZSoynrJgVVbu", "name": "StructuredOutput", "i